# Quality

- TypeScript `strict: true`. Never use `any`; use `unknown` and narrow.
- Never use `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error` unless unavoidable, with a comment.
- Explicit parameter types and return types.
- Small, focused PRs. One feature or fix per PR.
- No circular dependencies. Keep packages (`web`, `api`, `shared`, `ui`) at their boundaries.
- Do not commit secrets or `.env` files. Only `.env.example`.
- Validate API input with class-validator. Keep CORS origins in `CORS_ORIGINS`.
- Semantic HTML, keyboard access, visible focus, WCAG AA contrast.
- After changing OpenAPI controllers or DTOs, run `pnpm codegen` and commit the spec and Orval client.
